  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply the exponents and then we calculate the resulting power of \n$2.$\n:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({2}^{2})}^{3} & = \\\\ {2}^{(2\\cdot 3)} & = \\\\ {2}^{6} & = \\\\ 64\\end{aligned}\n$$",
